```

## Accessibility Checklist

### Implementation Checklist

- [ ] All interactive elements have `accessibilityRole`
- [ ] All interactive elements have `accessibilityLabel`
- [ ] Complex interactions have `accessibilityHint`
- [ ] Form inputs are properly labeled and associated
- [ ] Error messages use `accessibilityLiveRegion`
- [ ] Headings have proper hierarchy (`accessibilityLevel`)
- [ ] Focus management implemented for navigation
- [ ] Loading states announced to screen readers
- [ ] Modals properly trap focus
- [ ] Lists provide context about position and count
- [ ] Images have meaningful `alt` text or are marked decorative
- [ ] Color is not the only way to convey information
- [ ] Touch targets meet minimum size requirements (44pt/48dp)
- [ ] Text has sufficient color contrast (4.5:1 minimum)
- [ ] App works with screen readers (VoiceOver/TalkBack)
- [ ] App works with switch control
- [ ] Accessibility testing included in test suite

### Testing Methods

```bash
# ✅ Enable accessibility testing
yarn test --setupFilesAfterEnv='<rootDir>/jest.accessibility.setup.js'

# ✅ Manual testing with screen readers
# iOS: Enable VoiceOver in Settings > Accessibility
# Android: Enable TalkBack in Settings > Accessibility

# ✅ Use accessibility inspector tools
# iOS: Xcode Accessibility Inspector
# Android: Android Accessibility Scanner
```

